            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for a solemn promise, then the Latin for to bind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: iūsiūrandum, iūrisiūrandī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "iūsiūrandum, iūrisiūrandī — \"an oath\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Iūsiūrandum dedit sē reditūrum esse. He gave his oath that he would return."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "iūsiūrandum, iūrisiūrandī n.: both parts decline, iūre iūrandō, by oath. Built from iūs and iūrō, to swear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "iūsiūrandum is built from iūs \"right, law\" and iūrandum, the gerundive of iūrō \"to swear\" (Lewis & Short): a right that must be sworn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
