          "title": "You'll want to know: pacīscor, pacīscī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pacīscor, pacīscī — \"to strike a bargain, to come to terms\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cum hostibus dē pāce pacīscēbantur. They were bargaining with the enemy about peace."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: pacīscor, pacīscī, pactus sum, kin to pāx, peace. Cum aliquō pacīscī, to strike a bargain with someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pacīscor is built on an old verb pacō \"to come to terms\" with the ending -scō (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), and belongs with pāx \"peace\": to fix terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
